Chapter 36: The Hidden Blueprint
Beyond the heavy blast door in the back of Old Fixer Gideon’s shop lay a narrow corridor cut directly through raw subterranean granite.
The air grew cool and damp, smelling of heated copper, lead shielding, and old parchment. At the end of the corridor stood a second vault door, constructed from six-inch-thick anti-mana alloy.
Gideon stepped up to the terminal, pressing his cyborg palm against the scanner.
CLICK-BZZZZT.
"Most people think the Rust Vault is just a scrap heap for stolen cores," Gideon grunted, his mechanical eye whirring as he pushed the heavy door open. "They don't realize thirty years of rogue hunters passing through means thirty years of forgotten artifacts, illegal blue-prints, and skill scrolls brought back from the Wastes."
The vault opened into a well-lit stone chamber lined with reinforced glass display cases, heavy weapon racks, and rows of lead-lined book safes.
Kaelen stepped inside, his [Low-Light Spatial Perception] instantly scanning the room.
While the outer market was flooded with standard Guild-issued equipment, Gideon’s private vault held high-density items that had never been cataloged by municipal authorities: unregistered skill scrolls extracted from unmapped Rifts, ancient forging schematics from pre-Cataclysm ruins, and rare essence alloys.
"Take a look around," Gideon said, leaning against a worktable and lighting another dark cigar. "You've got nearly a million clean credits in your pocket, kid. If you're going down to my forge to melt those Tier-B Void-Scale plates, you might as well forge something worth the metal."
Kaelen walked past display cases housing high-tier daggers and heavy broadswords, his eyes entirely indifferent to standard weaponry. He didn't need a sword—his bare fists, backed by 101 Strength and 102 Agility, delivered more destructive kinetic force than any commercial blade.
He stopped in front of a small, lead-shielded glass case at the far end of the vault.
Inside sat two items: a yellowed, leather-bound forging manual sealed with an ancient brass clasp, and an obsidian skill scroll pulsing with faint, dark spatial energy.
[Item Identified: Blueprint — Scales of the Void-Dragon (Ancient Forging Schematic)]
 * Type: Concealed Armor Schematic (Sub-Dermal / Internal Mesh)
 * Requirements: Tier-B Void/Dragon Scale Plates, Kinetic Steel, High-Density Essence Catalyst.
 * Effect: Outlines the precise structural weave needed to forge a flexible, ultra-thin chest harness that integrates under ordinary clothing. Grants high-density physical absorption without adding weight or bulk.
[Item Identified: Skill Scroll — [Phantom Kinetic Cloak (Tier-B)]]
 * Type: Active Utility / Stealth Skill
 * Requirement: Aetheric Resonance 70+
 * Effect: Suppresses all outward mana signatures, physical heat, and heartbeat for 30 seconds. Renders the user completely invisible to biometric scanners, thermal sensors, and high-tier detection arrays while moving. (Cooldown: 45s).
Kaelen’s eyes sharpened.
The forging schematic was exactly what he needed. His current concealed gear covered his forearms (Kinetic-Void Bracers) and legs (Anchor-Greaves), but his chest remained protected only by his passive sub-dermal traits. A sub-dermal scale-mesh chest harness forged from Tier-B Void-Scale Hydra plates would make him virtually impervious to blunt and cutting attacks.
And the skill scroll—[Phantom Kinetic Cloak]—was the ultimate tool for his stealth operations. It would allow him to bypass Guild biometric scanners and high-tier detection arrays inside private dungeons without leaving a single trace.
"How much for these two?" Kaelen asked, pointing to the glass case.
Gideon blew a smoke ring, his mechanical eye clicking as it zoomed in on the case.
"That schematic came out of a Class-A Rift in the Outer Frontier ten years ago," Gideon said, his voice turning serious. "It’s designed for high-density scale weaving—impossible to forge without a high-tier flame and precision control. The skill scroll is an unregistered Tier-B stealth technique stolen from an illegal corporate lab."
Gideon tapped his ledger. "The pair will cost you 350,000 credits."
Without a single second of hesitation, Kaelen pulled the black credit token from his coat and tapped it against Gideon’s reader.
BEEP.
[Transaction Complete!]
 * Payment: 350,000 Credits
 * Remaining Balance: 619,000 Credits
[Acquired:]
 * Blueprint: Scales of the Void-Dragon
 * Skill Scroll: [Phantom Kinetic Cloak (Tier-B)]
Kaelen picked up the obsidian skill scroll. He didn't even wait to reach the forge.
He crushed the scroll in his palm.
The obsidian casing shattered into a stream of dark purple essence, flowing straight through his skin and into his nervous system.
[Skill Assimilation Triggered!]
 * Extracted Active Skill: [Phantom Kinetic Cloak (Tier-B)]
 * Skill stored successfully in Slot 2! (Replacing [Void-Step] or holding as secondary utility?)
Kaelen reviewed his skill configuration instantly:
[Active Skills Equipped (2 / 2 Slots)]
 * Slot 1: [Lightning-Phase Blitz (Tier-B)] — Offensive / Speed Boost
 * Slot 2: [Phantom Kinetic Cloak (Tier-B)] — Stealth / Sensor Erasure
(Note: [Void-Step (Tier-C Elite)] stored in reserve capacity).
Gideon unlocked the glass case, handed Kaelen the yellowed forging manual, and pointed toward a heavy steel elevator at the side of the vault.
"The Void-Forge is on Sub-Level 2," Gideon said, his tone carrying a quiet note of anticipation. "Anti-mana lead walls, a high-density plasma furnace, and an anvil made of compressed meteor iron. Take all the time you need, kid."
Kaelen took the schematic, pulled his hood low over his eyes, and stepped into the steel elevator.
The heavy steel doors closed with a deep, echoing thud as the elevator descended into the dark depths of the Rust Vault.
It was time to forge his ultimate armor.
